    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Меня только что молния ударила.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Lightning just struck me.' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'me', while 'to hit' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Лена, прости меня за всё.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Lena, forgive me for everything.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'Lena' and finishing on 'everything'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я тебя очень сильно люблю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I love you very much.' Notice how Russian expresses 'I' and 'like' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Elena answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Витя, что у тебя случилось?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vitya, what happened to you?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'what' before landing on 'happened'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я попал в большую беду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I got into big trouble.' The meaning hinges on 'I' working together with 'trouble' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Из-за меня сегодня погиб человек.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Because of me a person died today.' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'because of', while 'man' completes the thought. Elena answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Я приеду, мы всё решим.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will come over, we will solve everything.' The grammar packs 'I' and 'will sort out' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Прости, что скрывала от тебя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Forgive me for hiding it from you.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'forgive' and finishing on 'you'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "В Индии я была по заданию.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'In India I was on an assignment.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'India' and finishing on 'mission'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Ресторан был только моим прикрытием.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The restaurant was only my cover.' Elena anchors the line on 'restaurant', while 'cover' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Я должна следить за тобой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I have to watch over you.' The grammar packs 'I' and 'you' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Я постоянно подчищала за тобой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I constantly cleaned up after you.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'I' and finishing on 'you'. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
